# FINALPLAY11 -- the three files whose identity the launcher checks at startup.
#
# One truth, not two. The hashes used to be hardcoded inside launch-play.sh AND
# listed in FINAL_PRODUCTION.sha256, and the launcher was changed without the
# list: the manifest recorded 381f2350 for a script that hashed ff7be199. Now
# the launcher reads this file, so the pair cannot drift apart.
#
# Columns: mounted path, sha256, the file in the game directory it comes from.
# The MOUNTED path is what gets hashed -- what was asked for is not evidence of
# what is actually in place, and the class-B registry makes a half-updated pair
# worse than an outright failure to start.
/usr/bin/box86	ea3e367d71703039bd4a10b32e34b6c6f331b104f4316bc7180dfbf22052d120	box86-fp11
/usr/lib/wine/i386-windows/wined3d.dll	b35529b0ba4570bac910763f4c0180bac61d3648ab3a4033e718de5e31d02706	wined3d_fp11.dll
/usr/lib/wine/i386-unix/winewayland.so	51879e2d706d434e3bf140508e31493802d9506753a16b295be81df154f9f169	winewayland_dmabuf_prod.so
